  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 10 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes, 12 of 12 including the two existing `capitalize` tests.\n\nIt handles `đ`/`Đ` first, then strips diacritics and lowercases. Every run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes one hyphen, and leading and trailing hyphens are trimmed. It then cuts to 50 characters and removes any trailing hyphen the cut leaves.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- basic lowercasing and hyphenation\n- Vietnamese text including `đ`\n- other Latin diacritics\n- collapsing runs of symbols\n- trimming hyphens at the ends\n- empty and symbol-only input\n- digits\n- truncation at 50 characters, including a cut that would otherwise end in a hyphen\n- a slug of exactly 50 characters",
